WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.000
Pokemon Go is life…at least for the millions
of players who've swarmed the mobile game

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.210
since its launch.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.129
While developer Niantic plans on making the
game more robust, balanced, and stable, much

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:15.389
of the game hasn’t met players’ high expectations.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:16.539
Easy prey

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:20.240
One of the most important parts of Pokemon
is the ability to battle wild Pokemon.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.560
While Pokemon Go allows users to wander around
and go find a Gastly, there's really no fighting

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.560
involved.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.590
Instead, capturing wild pocket monsters has
become a game of ring toss.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.320
By bouncing a Pokeball off of a circle surrounding
your prey, you can attempt a capture.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.470
It's like an abridged version of a real Pokemon
experience.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.309
Rural ruminations

00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:40.820
Pokemon Go is catered to players in populated
and tech-savvy areas.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.760
Because it’s essentially a reskin of Niantic's
previous game, Ingress, every Pokestop is

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.069
a place which Ingress players had previously
marked.

00:00:47.069 --> 00:00:50.469
If you live in a small town, your local game
probably won’t have many stops.

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:54.440
None of this really fits Pokemon, where trainers
spend most of their time in forests, with

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.969
an occasional visit to a small town or a gym.

00:00:56.969 --> 00:01:00.710
Granted, wandering through the Wi-Fi-less
woods to play a mobile game isn't really safe,

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.690
but for now, Pokemon Go remains a game optimized
for cityfolk.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.000
Terrible tech

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.880
If your phone isn’t the newest model, or
it's slightly cloudy, or you're stuck on an

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.189
overloaded server, Go’s location services
have been shady.

00:01:13.189 --> 00:01:16.850
Players have spent days on end waiting for
their game to maintain a consistent connection.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.850
Even worse?

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:22.109
You finally find a distant Pokestop and you
inexplicably lose your GPS signal.

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:26.289
It's enough to make you want to stomp an Oddish…and
those guys are adorable.

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:27.289
Pay-to-play

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:31.590
Because Go is a mobile app, microtransactions
are expected.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:35.829
But because it's an actively competitive mobile
app, those with cash can quickly rise to the

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.829
top.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:40.210
Wallet warriors are an issue with just about
every multiplayer online game made for smart

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.439
phones, but Pokemon is a property that's basically
intended for kids.

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:48.100
Putting a paywall in front of a little aspiring
Ash Ketchum just feels nasty.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.609
Lousy launch

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.359
Niantic's servers just can’t handle the
app’s traffic.

00:01:52.359 --> 00:01:56.399
Games sometimes freeze immediately after important
captures...if you can log on at all.

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:59.640
While portions of the app have smoothed out,
there are still plenty of aspects that simply

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.510
don't work consistently enough to offer a
truly enjoyable experience.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.439
Everything still feels like it's in beta mode,
but the future still looks exciting.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:08.610
Hackemon

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.570
As with any competitive app, there are already
cheaters out there.

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:15.950
Within days of release, it was easy to find
files helping players obtain endless currency,

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.210
level up their Pokemon without any effort,
and visit local gyms without ever leaving

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.210
their bathroom.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:25.580
One would hope that the moral lessons of Pokemon
would somehow carry over into real-world Pokemon

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:30.470
Go etiquette, but as long as there are people
who can't be trusted, there'll always disappointment

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.850
and distrust.

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:32.850
Thanks for watching!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.870
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.830
And leave us a comment to let us know what’s
disappointed you in Pokemon Go...

